Package: preENM
Type: Package
Title: Data Preparation and Model Selection for Ecological Niche and Species
    Distribution Models
Version: 2.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Kamil", "Konowalik", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "kamil.konowalik@gmail.com")
Description: Tools for the steps around fitting ecological niche models /
    species distribution models (ENM/SDM) with any software. Data
    preparation: transparent, rule-based filtering of occurrence records
    (especially GBIF downloads), including detection of atlas grid data,
    coordinate precision, settlements, sea, range and climatic outliers, with
    optional tests from 'CoordinateCleaner'; delimitation of the accessible
    area (M) from a data-derived linking distance, with room for expert
    additions; one record per raster cell; and random background point sets. Model evaluation and selection: the
    simultaneous use of the area under the ROC curve (AUC) and the mean
    absolute error (MAE) proposed in Konowalik and Nosol (2021)
    <doi:10.1038/s41598-020-80062-1>, the true skill statistic and the
    continuous Boyce index; spatial block cross-validation; temporal
    validation of hindcasts against dated (e.g. fossil) records; and model
    selection by conventional minimum values or Pareto optimality on
    user-chosen metrics, with bootstrap estimates of selection robustness.
